{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Phase 2 done. Fix pushed as Gerrit change 1805 (https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/1805).\n\nRED->GREEN proof (no live creds): tests/unit/test_completion_bank_observer_forwarding.py.\n- Before fix (narrow stub signature): raises the EXACT production error 'make_observed_upsert.<locals>.observed_upsert() got an unexpected keyword argument evidence_sufficient' (and the same for seeded) — 3 failed.\n- After fix (forward **kwargs): 3 passed. Also verified the bookkeeping (first tool-write recording) is preserved.\n\nFix: extracted the bank-observation stub into a shared, live-dep-free helper tests/_bank_observer.py::make_observed_upsert that forwards every kwarg other than source verbatim via **kwargs (so evidence_sufficient, seeded, and any future upsert kwarg flow through). The live eval tests/external/test_completion_banking_behavior_0707.py now uses the helper. Production code unchanged.\n\nValidation: ruff check + format-check clean on all 3 files; mypy clean on the new files (CI mypy scope is src/rebar + scripts only, tests/ excluded). Ran tests/unit -k 'completion or banking or recovery or verdict' = 512 passed, 3 skipped, 1 pre-existing unrelated failure (test_commit_and_push_tickets_branch_heldout — environmental git safe.bareRepository='explicit', reproduces identically on origin/main).\n\nSibling sweep: observed_upsert is the only upsert monkeypatch stub in the completion-verifier tests; no other *_upsert closures with the same threading gap. No siblings to file.\n\nNext: await LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1 on change 1805, Submit, then close."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786773928775855001,"uuid":"931e1ee5-13